<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n58463" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοιρᾰν-έω</span></b> , poet. Verb, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be lord</i> or <i>master, rule,
			command</i>, in <i><span class="en">Hom., 1</span></i>. of a
			military leader, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὣς ὅ γε κοιρανέων δίεπε στρατόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.207
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				4.250
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάχην ἀνὰ κοιρανέοντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					5.824
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλεμον κάτα κοιρανέουσιν</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				332
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of a king in
			peace, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λυκίην κάτα κοιρανέουσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					12.318
				</span></i>
			; of the suitors (princes) in Ithaca, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				1.247
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> later c.
			gen., <i>to be lord of</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				331
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				214
			</span></i>: c. dat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοῖσι κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					49
				</span></i>
			; 
				Ep.
			impf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοιρανέεσκεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.998
				</span></i>
			: abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν νῦν κοιρανοῦντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					958
				</span></i>
			: c. acc., <i>lead, arrange</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χορούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					14.9
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Del.</u>
				167
			</span></i>.</div>
